# legendary — built FROM SOURCE via a novadeck-owned PKGBUILD (packages/legendary/PKGBUILD), NOT
# fetched from the holo monorepo: legendary is an AUR-only package, absent from holo core and extra
# aarch64 (checked against build/snapshot.pin), so there is no repo row to resolve and no upstream
# PKGBUILD to pull. Same "local PKGBUILD" form as packages/f3/source.pin.
#
# Why: the Epic half of alien-games milestone 1 (.claude/plans/alien-games.plan.md). legendary is
# the CLI that authenticates against Epic, lists what an account owns and downloads it. Nothing in
# the image calls it yet — this milestone lands inert on purpose.
#
# Version: 0.20.43, the Heroic fork's latest. See the PKGBUILD header for why the fork and not
# derrod/legendary.
#
# It is pure Python, so arch=('any') and there is no FEX anywhere in this path — the x86_64
# artifacts upstream publishes are a convenience for Deck users, not a constraint on us.
#
# PATCH 0001 adds `sync-saves --dry-run`: print what a sync would do (legendary's own
# SaveGameStatus, the save path, each side's newest time, the last sync) as one JSON line per game,
# and change nothing. Cloud saves need the verdict BEFORE anything moves, because a real sync with
# -y only logs a conflict, stores --save-path in installed.json, and deletes the local save files
# before it fetches the cloud's (.claude/plans/epic-cloud-saves.plan.md design §1). Also sent
# upstream; drop it once a legendary release carries --dry-run. check-dry-run.py (a local source)
# runs from build() against the patched tree, because the overlay build runs makepkg with --nocheck.
#
# PATCH 0002 makes a game's CloudIncludeList / CloudExcludeList select the same files for an upload
# and a download's clean-up, IN ANY CASE, as on the Epic client's case-insensitive file systems. On
# Linux fnmatch was case-sensitive: Fallout's SAVE.DAT never reached the cloud (HW 2026-11-19). The
# download also read the lists unstripped, which alone kept a clean-up from deleting MASTER.DAT once
# "*.dat" matches it, so both are fixed together; and an empty item ("LocalData/,") no longer
# excludes every file. check-save-filters.py runs legendary's real upload and download against a
# copy of Fallout's Epic install. Also for upstream, with 0001.
#
# Fields (see packages/README.md):
#   name           pkgname (must match the PKGBUILD); also the work/ build-dir + repo entry
#   pkgbuild_local path (relative to this dir) to the checked-in PKGBUILD to build
#   pkgrel_suffix  numeric suffix appended to the PKGBUILD's pkgrel so pacman prefers our build
#   patches        under patches/, applied -p1 right after prepare()'s first cd
#   local_sources  files the PKGBUILD's own source=() names, staged beside it
#
# To bump legendary: edit pkgver + sha256sums in packages/legendary/PKGBUILD, re-audit the runtime
# imports (the depends list below the header is derived from them, not from install_requires — see
# the PKGBUILD), re-check that patches 0001 and 0002 still apply (or are upstream), and `make relock`.
name: legendary
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
pkgrel_suffix: 1
patches: 0001-sync-saves-add-dry-run.patch 0002-sync-saves-match-save-filters-in-any-case.patch
local_sources: check-dry-run.py check-save-filters.py
